{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261114-evidence2","scope":"Three bounded number-state learning panels, structure-source handoff into explicit representation calculations, and an official Cu thermal-file workflow.","counts":{"oscillatorLessons":3,"oscillatorPlacements":3,"cuInputCellAtoms":4,"cuRows":251},"hooks":{"scattering-temperature":["ladder-weights"],"polaron-hamiltonian":["vacuum-motion"],"polaron-truncation":["finite-boundary"]},"verification":["Independent number-state sums and matrices check amplitudes, probabilities, separately weighted tails, microscopic reverse transitions and finite-boundary commutators against the fixed references and the existing Python API.","Course integration preserves disclosures, unfinished responses, notes and original calculator drafts; explicit copying preserves the exact chosen temperature and waits for manual calculation.","Strict source metadata preserves file/text hash identity, tolerances, basis/origin and wavevector transforms and single/double-valued selection through workbench export and explicitly saved research records. Changed requests cannot inherit unrelated source metadata.","Official Cu source bytes, lossless XZ decompression, input-cell normalization and all thermal rows are checked. Import loading, replacement, cancellation and stale completion are exercised through actual form handlers."],"boundaries":["Fixed teaching references do not introduce a general oscillator or scattering solver. Holstein vacuum and numerical truncation panels do not infer a finite-temperature polaron state.","A source checksum identifies the parsed source; it is not an electronic-structure calculation or magnetic-order detector. Imported metadata cannot independently reverify absent original bytes. Numerical representation validity and standard-label coverage remain separate.","Cu thermal_properties data describe one official calculated four-atom input cell at one volume. They do not supply eigenvectors, measured data, full quasi-harmonic volume predictions or a newly performed material calculation.","This release covers three learning hooks and representative source workflows. Broader curriculum depth, diagnosis and authentic workflows for every tool family remain open."],"files":{"GOAL-ROADMAP.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":44691,"sha256":"ad81ca1052c1ff630e574f71da40955999bbb2b553f8c11e0bf8518a894ecb2a"},"dist/app.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":97824,"sha256":"eaa92a81e16993d93e14e376f8b6962c697e8009d597ac6b40aef8d362ed6ce9"},"dist/bridges-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":17143,"sha256":"ab62e4088853f8820f4a835bc5c95b3888da6f0d74e34098887f491bfd5310db"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-LICENSE.txt":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":1470,"sha256":"2ce26839c8b70d28765d73e934cc1a979d896d8d228d30694fdd9a92e94d43a9"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":41975,"sha256":"1c9e6edeeded194fc7eebe9c4f4bd6e88728b48ea4f530a033240f8394267bf1"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml.xz":{"normalization":"raw-bytes","bytes":4900,"sha256":"36c87fc5560cc7815cd9d97105830c00cffa4a3a2fb486235d7976bc493ebb1f"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-source.json":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":2907,"sha256":"903330e565a126b3e8d30b09099ce1a352fbf0703c9d98e4cf2344e56941763f"},"dist/docs/cu-thermal-example.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4040,"sha256":"69155f09dba2ab02a9a59e71a7f55b2a16ebf5bf177b295c1144eb892027a017"},"dist/index.html":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":7460,"sha256":"cc79fffff468e902445d4ff829be7288d49e8bbbc1b65ce3781473e7878c8131"},"dist/learning-bridge-host.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4616,"sha256":"b549c0f3268b4ccf3b2e801bf6a5cb91d2be1a666903fb0e03b70f26467b70e8"},"dist/material-notebook.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":24765,"sha256":"6f2aa00927ae19bec85486460a3bb7b7d0a59e5feb403c14f0623d8054cdae16"},"dist/material-research-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf